From eea98c9699f1f7bf7e43af0d211f244f432d0f09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 3 <phase3@openwch.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 02:05:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] RISC-V: match WCH fast interrupt EVT frames

Returning ISR objects in v3b-pioc, v3c-led, and v4bc-pmp differ because
pristine GCC rejects WCH-Interrupt-fast and emits ordinary returns.
Accept the exact WCH spelling while retaining its incomplete warning list,
model hardware-saved caller GPRs, preserve software callee and FPR saves,
suppress t0 and FCSR traffic, and emit the existing machine-mode mret.

The hardware-saved set is exactly the call-clobbered GPRs, and ra needs no
test of its own: this port marks ra both fixed and call-clobbered
(riscv.h, "x0, ra, sp, gp, and tp are fixed" and "The call RTLs themselves
clobber ra"), so call_used_or_fixed_reg_p already returns true for it.

Register renaming stays on the upstream interrupt contract, under which a
rename target must already be live and therefore covered by the prologue.
Relaxing it for the hardware-saved set was measured to move the observed
reset-value chain in five non-returning CoreMark handlers from a5 to a
previously unused t0, so a later patch in this series adds the regression
test that pins the contract instead.

Behavior specification:
  analysis/toolchain/wch-gcc-toolchain-survey.md section 5.5
  ref/wch-isa-research/isa/custom/qingke-custom-isa.md section 4.2
  ref/wch-isa-research/isa/custom/wch-custom-isa-reference.md section 6.3

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/riscv/riscv.cc (TH_INT_INTERRUPT): Exclude WCH fast
	interrupts.
	(struct machine_function): Add wch_fast_interrupt_p.
	(riscv_handle_type_attribute): Accept the WCH-Interrupt-fast
	spelling.
	(riscv_wch_fast_interrupt_type_p): New function.
	(riscv_wch_fast_interrupt_saved_reg_p): New function.
	(riscv_save_reg_p): Do not software-save what the WCH fast
	interrupt hardware prologue already saved.
	(riscv_compute_frame_info): Skip the interrupt CSR and large-frame
	reservation for WCH fast interrupts.
	(riscv_for_each_saved_reg): Do not save the prologue temporary for
	WCH fast interrupts.
	(riscv_set_current_function): Set wch_fast_interrupt_p.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-epilogue-live.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-float.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-leaf.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-nonleaf.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-warning.c: New test.
